{"name":"Mount Eden","hex":"#e7efe0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mount","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hill or mountain.","Any of seven fleshy prominences in the palm of the hand, taken to represent the influences of various heavenly bodies."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An animal, usually a horse, used to ride on.","A car, bicycle, or motorcycle used for racing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mount"},{"term":"eden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Eden (“a paradise”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eden"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mount Eden","blocks":[{"text":"Mount Eden is a suburb in Auckland, New Zealand, whose name honours George Eden, 1st Earl of Auckland. It is 4 kilometres (2.5 mi) south of the Central Business District (CBD). Mt Eden Road winds its way around the side of Mount Eden Domain and continues to weave back and forth as it descends into the valley; it runs south from Eden Terrace to Three Kings. Mt Eden village centre is located roughly between Valley Road and Grange Road. The domain is accessible on foot from many of the surrounding streets, and by vehicle from Mt Eden Road. The central focus of the suburb is Maungawhau / Mount Eden, a dormant volcano whose summit is the highest natural point on the Auckland isthmus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Mount_Eden_from_Maungawhau_%28Mount_Eden%29.jpg/330px-Mount_Eden_from_Maungawhau_%28Mount_Eden%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Eden","wikidata":"Q477145"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Mt_Eden%2C_Auckland2.jpg/500px-Mt_Eden%2C_Auckland2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Mt_Eden%2C_Auckland2.jpg/500px-Mt_Eden%2C_Auckland2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mount Eden (left, beyond Alexandra Park) from One Tree Hill","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMt_Eden%2C_Auckland2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Mount_Eden_Road%2C_Mount_Eden%2C_Auckland_%2821499756170%29.jpg/500px-Mount_Eden_Road%2C_Mount_Eden%2C_Auckland_%2821499756170%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Mount_Eden_Road%2C_Mount_Eden%2C_Auckland_%2821499756170%29.jpg/1280px-Mount_Eden_Road%2C_Mount_Eden%2C_Auckland_%2821499756170%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Mount_Eden_Road%2C_Mount_Eden%2C_Auckland_%2821499756170%29.jpg/500px-Mount_Eden_Road%2C_Mount_Eden%2C_Auckland_%2821499756170%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mount Eden Road in the early 1900s","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMount_Eden_Road%2C_Mount_Eden%2C_Auckland_(21499756170).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Mount_Eden_Road.jpg/500px-Mount_Eden_Road.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Mount_Eden_Road.jpg/1280px-Mount_Eden_Road.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Mount_Eden_Road.jpg/500px-Mount_Eden_Road.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mount Eden in 2010","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMount_Eden_Road.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/NZ_AK_Dominion_Road_Methodist_Church_%282%29.jpg/500px-NZ_AK_Dominion_Road_Methodist_Church